<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Bakr ibn Umar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1087">1087</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Bakr ibn Umar was an Almoravid leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamtuna">Lamtuna</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berbers</a> in the eleventh century. After leaving northern operations to his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a>, he returned to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> and campaigned in the south. He is associated with Almoravid pressure on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a> and with spreading the movement's influence in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-bakr-ibn-umar.jpg" alt="Abu Bakr ibn Umar" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: alif · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abu_Bakr_ibn_Omar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
